    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Sweet, spicy, and on the table in about 45 minutes. The glaze here is three pantry ingredients in equal parts — Dijon, honey, and sriracha — brushed onto sushi-grade salmon, crusted with sesame seeds, and baked until the sugars catch and caramelize. It lands on creamy coconut jasmine rice with a bright mango salsa, cool cucumber, and edamame, so every bite has heat, sweetness, acid, and crunch at once.</p><p>We built this recipe around Seatopia <a href=\"/products/atlantic-salmon-2x-6oz-portions\" title=\"Seatopia Atlantic Salmon\">Atlantic Salmon</a> from <a href=\"/pages/bakkafrost-atlantic-salmon\" title=\"Bakkafrost, Faroe Islands\">Bakkafrost</a> in the Faroe Islands — 6 oz skin-off, sushi-grade portions that go from thawed to done in 10–12 minutes and are lab tested to the <a href=\"/pages/why-clean-seafood-matters\" title=\"Why Clean Seafood Matters\">Seatopia Standard™</a> for mercury, microplastics, and nutrient density.</p><p>This one is a collaboration with <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/runningonveggies/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Lottie Bildirici on Instagram\">Lottie Bildirici</a> of <em>Running on Veggies</em> — holistic nutritionist, Ironman, marathoner, and author of the best-selling cookbook of the same name. Lottie builds food around how it makes you perform, which is exactly the brief here: a bowl that eats like a treat and still loads you up with marine omega-3s, fiber, and slow carbs.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_intro"
      ],
