    "game_plan": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "step_rice": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/hot-honey-salmon-bowl-hero.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 0",
            "heading": "Start the coconut rice",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Rinse 1 cup of jasmine rice until the water runs clear — this is what keeps it from going gluey. Add ½ cup full-fat coconut milk, 1 cup water, and ½ tsp kosher salt. Bring to a boil, drop to low, cover, and simmer 15 minutes. Then let it sit covered off the heat for 10 more minutes before fluffing with a fork.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "step_glaze": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/hot-honey-salmon-glaze-closeup.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 2",
            "heading": "Glaze the salmon and walk away",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Whisk 2 Tbsp Dijon, 2 Tbsp honey, and 2 Tbsp sriracha. Coat both fillets evenly, scatter 2 tsp sesame seeds over the top, and leave them to marinate at least 30 minutes while you handle everything else. The mustard helps the glaze cling instead of sliding off in the oven.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "step_salsa": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/hot-honey-mango-salsa-ingredients.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 10",
            "heading": "Build the mango salsa",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Dice one ripe mango, one red bell pepper, ¼ red onion, and ½ tomato. Add ½ cup chopped cilantro, the juice of one lime, and salt and pepper to taste. Jalapeño is optional. Toss it and let it sit — the salt draws out juice and it genuinely improves in the 20 minutes it waits.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "step_assemble": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/hot-honey-salmon-bowl-overhead.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 32",
            "heading": "Bake, then assemble",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Bake the salmon at 400°F for 10–12 minutes, until it flakes easily with a fork. Divide the coconut rice among three bowls, lay the salmon alongside, and pile on the mango salsa, cooked edamame, and sliced cucumber. Finish with a hard squeeze of lime, extra cilantro, and a pinch more sesame.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "step_rice",
        "step_glaze",
        "step_salsa",
        "step_assemble"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.timeline.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "image_ratio": "square",
        "image_ratio_mobile": "landscape",
        "heading": "The 45-minute game plan",
        "heading_size": "title-md",
        "heading_alignment": "text-left md:items-end md:flex-row",
        "heading_tag": "h2",
        "subheading": "",
        "description": "<p>Work in this order and everything lands hot at the same time. The salmon marinates while the rice simmers and you chop the salsa — no step is wasted waiting on another.</p>",
